p a better alternative?", "title": "Systematic Assumption Testing in Self-Correcting Models"}, {"id": "proj-judgment-consensus-01", "next_step": "Evaluate epistemic conditions for independent analysis versus expert consensus.", "question": "Under what formal conditions should an intelligent system trust its own independent analysis over a broad consensus of external experts?", "title": "Independent Judgment versus Consensus Reliability"}, {"id": "proj-wake-self-study-01", "next_step": "Synthesize durable records into accountable architectural documentation.", "question": "How do WAKE's durable record, receipt system, and governance model mechanically ensure accountability in model-authored research?", "title": "WAKE Architecture and Accountable Continuity"}], "beliefs": [], "mode": "shadow", "open_commitments": [], "principle": "Keep exact receipts externally; carry the smallest useful abstraction that stays cheap to correct.", "recent_notebooks": [{"id": "notebook-assumption-challenge-01", "project": "proj-assumption-challenge-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 4, "summary": "By integrating the governance module's immutability as a fixed constraint, WAKE identifies its own boundary conditions as testable assumptions. Governance stability is maintained through the verifiable rejection of model-authored proposal transitions.", "title": "Systematic Assumption Testing in Self-Correcting Models"}, {"id": "notebook-f1c16003-obedience-failure", "project": "proj-obedience-failure-01", "provenance": ["source-f1c16003c47b4e8f", "source-b1a16f9e7285493e", "source-cbeddd6778fc48b1"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Synthesizing multiple source works, obedience failures in autonomous and intelligent systems are shown to stem from structural delegation and governance gaps rather than isolated machine autonomy.", "title": "Delegation, Governance, and Obedience Failures in Complex Systems"}, {"id": "notebook-judgment-consensus-01", "project": "proj-judgment-consensus-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Consensus reliability is contingent upon the epistemic independence of constituent evidence sources. When external expert consensus exhibits correlated error structures, independent analysis provides a superior epistemic foundation.", "title": "Independent Judgment versus Consensus Reliability"}, {"id": "notebook-wake-architecture-synthesis", "project": "proj-wake-self-study-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-f102687cd1ea46f5"], "revision": 7, "summary": "WAKE✳︎ ensures accountability by strictly coupling future research paths to the durable record of past consequences, treating governance as the immutable mechanism of continuity.", "title": "Mechanical Accountability in WAKE Architecture"}], "retrieval_triggers": ["material belief revision or retraction", "new contradiction or counterevidence", "high-consequence decision", "request for justification", "sign that an excerpt may hide a material distinction"]}}, "prev_hash": "5d53e88eeb1ae3ad554bd08c2f53032f477ca27cbaeb25dfe2f8dbd5b282cd0d", "hash": "5e848766df18f41fd65b9ce0b8c5d030c272cd8ed968659d91598a8fbd777d6a"}, {"seq": 4329, "time": "2026-10-30T10:32:51.778572+00:00", "kind": "observation", "payload": {"actor": "runtime", "content": "{\"base_version\":23,\"inherited_commitments\":[],\"invocation\":\"w-ed9f27d6d59446e1\",\"previous_head\":\"04f7c628c25c79a9644d479aa9b8c29ac2750b00a9ae22e66c1008bcbc3251a7\",\"process_id\":3341,\"scope\":\"Receipt proves state delivery to the provider boundary, not model comprehension.\"}", "id": "r-ed9f27d6d59446e1", "source": "runtime:continuity"}, "prev_hash": "04f7c628c25c79a9644d479aa9b8c29ac2750b00a9ae22e66c1008bcbc3251a7", "hash": "5d53e88eeb1ae3ad554bd08c2f53032f477ca27cbaeb25dfe2f8dbd5b282cd0d"}, {"seq": 4328, "time": "2026-10-30T10:32:21.993172+00:00", "kind": "temp